{"kind":"report","text":"Approved member/presence design draft 3 at exact c16fe0aa3a5d22e7cc5b44030122ee524b813a43, tree 851ec653835f67438e95674aa0676fb95634aebf. Primary c22f6671 read FIRST IN FULL, all 424 lines, with the complete change from draft 2. No further findings. This is design approval under request 0cc1aab4/promise 45d75285, not runtime or visual implementation acceptance.\n\nConclusion 1 — fidelity: F3 and F4 of d273ec2d are addressed. Every recorded presence entry number now comes from an explicit report fact required from the second G3 presence item: a Site-under fact ref for arrive/leave, written using the existing self form. The note distinguishes that fact's entry position from the item's revision and opening position, supplies “report entry unavailable” when the fact is absent, and carries the requirement into B3 and the late-opening witness. Removal provenance has three separate outcomes: a matching removal in a complete window, a complete captured window with no match, and refused/failed/incomplete bounded reads. Only the second may say “not in the last 100 entries”; the third says “removal entry unavailable,” preserves known identity/state and performs no wider lookup.\n\nThe earlier F1/F2 corrections remain intact: the occupancy source is the second G3 application's persistent Site item, not today's last-100 activity log; the room item maps to the full subject, one-room and wrong-room-leave semantics are stated, and B3 starts after that head lands. Recorded expressions carry no live status, note, freshness or lease. Removed state is shown from the member item alone; optional provenance is confined to the record screen.\n\nConclusion 2 — correctness and witnesses: checked the native Fact field/ref-slot and self-effect forms, existing fact-ref precedent, item revision fold, membership remove-member effect, projection window contract and inherited live presence declaration. The report fact is a supported native form and does not require treating an item revision as a fact or scanning history. Source/design traces cover late opening beyond the activity window, a subsequent move whose revision differs from its journal position, a missing report fact, a wrong-room leave, an old removal and refused history access. These are explicit design/source checks, not executed native witnesses. The three-layer unavailable policies, bounded 32-member table/overflow, controller attribution, typed party/signer resolution and package member-open-only API remain coherent. Kit-only membership/presence writes remain an authority boundary to implement and test, not hostile-script isolation. B1/B2 can use existing recorded APIs; B3 requires the separately implemented persistent source; B4 waits for the live executor. Enter/Renew/Leave still require actual session/ownership/generation/expected judgments, and no lease extends by reading or transport activity alone.\n\nConclusion 3 — validation cost and limits: only this note changes from draft 2 and from its explicitly declared authored Main 4d8c878c4c40f6d4399f2bcf5567125bb3ba1bc8/tree e568c5d498e974bacd49e135e452e8b5a24edbee. Independently compared all 2240 candidate Git mode/blob leaves; 2239 base leaves are unchanged. This older authored base is explicit; later Main runtime differences are not new changes in this design head. Whitespace and all 16 relative links pass. The exact-path artifact query is exhausted with one fresh candidate artifact and native prepare confirms the assigned implementation/primary. Source and tests are unchanged, so docs/testing.md's documentation-only exception applies: no full gate or whole suite repeated. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-member-presence-draft3-4kri12u1 has exact note.md and validation.json; note SHA256 9b26c581c36478d5bf340204498b573bbba51e0768083bea7159596f9d319f74.\n\nD1 mockups, B1–B3 source/runtime/browser acceptance, the second G3 source's exact provisioning/state/act steps and report-fact witnesses, B4 live behavior, deployment and publication remain separate. The illustrative presence trace is a design obligation, not an observation that the future source has run. Landing this note must preserve current Main runtime and take only its reviewed documentation change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c22f66716b8f1fe455ac4d797c1cd4f8875773c2","binding":"assigned","head":"c16fe0aa3a5d22e7cc5b44030122ee524b813a43","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4820ab2dca4bea5995ec326d8cde8e1f07db6c69\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45d75285ba181142cec9f66a640987a0b44093bc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:025b7ccd5bed1ade475fc2432c8642724190b691","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}